      "description": "Career Opportunities | Make it McKendree! For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Adjunct Faculty for MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (Professional and Ethical Issues) | Make it McKendree! page has loaded. Adjunct Faculty for MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (Professional and Ethical Issues) | Make it McKendree! page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Career Opportunities Menu Career Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Make it McKendree! powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Adjunct Faculty for MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (Professional and Ethical Issues) Print Apply ﻿ Adjunct Faculty for MA in Clinical Mental Health Counseling (Professional and Ethical Issues) Salary See Position Description Location Lebanon, IL Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 202600023 Department Academic Affairs Division Health Professions Opening Date 07/17/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits McKendree University, located in Lebanon, IL and home of the Bearcats, invites qualified applicants to join our team. McKendree University offers a competitive compensation and benefits package and the opportunity to influence the future leaders of tomorrow. The mission of McKendree University is to provide a high-quality educational experience to outstanding students. We guide our students in the pursuit of academic excellence, which will prepare them for leadership roles in our society. To achieve this end we encourage broader vision, enriched purpose, engagement with community, commitment to responsible citizenship, openness to new ideas and dedication to lifelong learning. In keeping with our history and traditions, we provide our students with a rigorous, broadly based liberal arts curriculum joined with specialization in a specific discipline. Position Summary and Key Responsibilities Support the academic learning of MA students in the counseling program.  This position is responsible for teaching in a face-to-face format. Area of specialization is related to Professional and Ethical Issues in Counseling. Courses are offered in 8-week and 16-week sessions during the fall, spring, and summer terms. Qualifications Required Qualifications: A Master’s degree in counseling or a closely related field. A Doctorate degree is preferred. Clinical licensure (LCPC preferable). A record of dedication to teaching with face-to-face and hybrid instructional experience. Preferred Qualifications: Prior college teaching experience. Work Conditions Regular pay rate: $2,145.00 for each 3-hour course, per semester.  Higher rates may apply for larger course enrollments, labs, or other duties. Online/remote teaching opportunities may exist dependent on the needs of the course. Applicants interested in online/remote opportunities must reside in the following states: IL, CA, FL, TN, KY. Required Application Materials Cover Letter Resume/CV Copies of transcripts (official required upon hire) Three letters of reference. Equal Opportunity Employer McKendree University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and other statuses protected by law. This extends to all aspects of the employment relationship, including recruiting, hiring, training, on-the-job treatment, promotion, layoff, and termination. Part-time employees are not eligible for benefits. Part-time employees who work an average of 20 hours per week may be eligible for our deferred compensation plan. Part-time faculty and staff also enjoy: - Discounted tuition after 1 year of employment !  Spouses and dependents under the age of 26 are also eligible for discounted undergraduate level courses. - Complimentary or discounted tickets to our premier performing arts venue, presenting world class dance, drama, classical music and jazz. - Complimentary tickets for Athletic events. - Discounts at the McKendree University Bookstore. Employer McKendree University Address 701 College Rd Lebanon, Illinois, 62254 Website http://www.mckendree.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Career Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    a